## Running it — language-aware `bin/00_config`

Rather than a separate Python bin script, `week1_baseline/bin/00_config` becomes
language-aware: it picks Ruby or Python based on a flag/env var, defaulting to
one of them (TBD which — suggest Ruby stays default since it's the established
baseline, Python opts in via `--python` / `BOUKENSHA_LANG=python`). Sketch:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
lang="${BOUKENSHA_LANG:-ruby}"
[[ "${1:-}" == "--python" ]] && lang="python"

case "$lang" in
  ruby)
    cd "$(dirname "$0")/../ruby/00_config"
    bundle exec ruby examples/example.rb
    ;;
  python)
    cd "$(dirname "$0")/../python/00_config"
    uv run python examples/example.py
    ;;
  *)
    echo "unknown BOUKENSHA_LANG: $lang" >&2; exit 1 ;;
esac
```

## `.yaml` / `.yml` fix

The Python port fixes the extension bug noted in the Ruby README's
"Considerations" section: `Config` will look for `settings.yaml` first, then
fall back to `settings.yml`, instead of hardcoding `.yaml` only. (This is a
Python-port-only fix — the Ruby side keeps its current hardcoded-`.yaml`
behavior unless/until a separate change addresses it there too.)

## Tests

No `pytest` suite for this port — matches the Ruby side, which only has the
`examples/example.py` smoke test (1:1 port of `example.rb`'s behavior and
printed output).

